          "id": "103917"
        },
        "body": "Hi @mfenniak. Thank you for your work on the plugin architecture. I test and use it actively with your [runner-systemd-nspawn](https://codeberg.org/mfenniak/runner-systemd-nspawn) plugin and have created a few feature requests specific to that plugin there:\r\n\r\n1. [Use machines of any type (raw images, directories, etc.)](https://codeberg.org/mfenniak/runner-systemd-nspawn/issues/61)\r\n2. [User namespacing, --private-users=pick or --private-users=managed](https://codeberg.org/mfenniak/runner-systemd-nspawn/issues/71)\r\n3. [Consider using --notify-ready=true and avoid checking multi-user.target and network-online.target](https://codeberg.org/mfenniak/runner-systemd-nspawn/issues/72)\r\n4. [Consider allowing container: options: to pass through to faciliate testing of options](https://codeberg.org/mfenniak/runner-systemd-nspawn/issues/78)\r\n\r\nI agree with @roman-eidenai about the current options/defaults being targeted toward docker."
      },
