          "id": "103321"
        },
        "body": "@Cysioland wrote in https://code.forgejo.org/forgejo/runner/issues/1777#issue-14934:\r\n\r\n> I cannot reproduce on next because of there being no runner (unless I'm doing something wrong).\r\n\r\nYou should be able to attach a runner yourself. But it's rarely necessary.\r\n\r\n> The issue is that before validation of workflows has been introduced (so, a long time ago), I was able to select which matrix steps to run through `workflow_dispatch` parameters, now it's impossible.\r\n\r\nThe problem is the usage of `matrix` in `if:`. `matrix` is not [available there](https://forgejo.org/docs/latest/user/actions/reference/#availability). GitHub [agrees](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/contexts#context-availability). It's unlikely that we'll add `matrix` there because it will cause precedence problems.\r\n\r\nI don't have an idea for a workaround right now."
      },
